<%# The AI protocol (doc/ki_bereich_navigation_plan.md S5, L13/E5).

    Wann, wer, was — and nothing invented for it. Every row's wording already exists:
    Activity#action_text renders the short verb (activities.organisation.*),
    Activity#message the sentence with the actor in it (activities.messages.organisation.*).
    Both were written by P4e and S0 for a trail nobody could see yet.

    ⚠️ Neither method fails loudly. #message rescues I18n::MissingInterpolationArgument
    into "Actor — Verb", and #action_text humanises an unknown key, so a MISSING text
    looks like plausible copy rather than like a defect. That is why the keys are pinned
    by spec/locales/ai_protocol_verbs_guard_spec.rb against the backend tree instead of
    being trusted here.

    The detail line below the sentence carries what the sentence cannot: the jurisdiction
    the organisation moved BETWEEN. That is the field the whole chapter exists for ("EU
    ist Standard, US die bewusste Abweichung"), it is stored raw in the payload precisely
    so no row freezes today's wording, and it is resolved to a label at render time. %>
<div>
  <%= render 'organisations/shared/ai_area_header',
        title: t('views.organisations.ai_overview.protocol.title') %>

  <p class="mb-6 max-w-3xl text-sm text-cream-600">
    <%= t('views.organisations.ai_overview.protocol.intro') %>
  </p>

  <% if @entries.any? %>
    <%# <ol>, not <ul>: the order IS the information on this page. %>
    <ol class="space-y-3">
      <% @entries.each do |entry| %>
        <li class="rounded-lg border-2 border-ink bg-white p-4 shadow-[3px_3px_0_0_#000000]">
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-x-4 gap-y-1">
            <span class="inline-flex items-center rounded-md border border-cream-300 bg-cream-100 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-bold text-cream-900"
                  data-protocol-action="<%= entry.action %>">
              <%= entry.action_text %>
            </span>
            <time datetime="<%= entry.created_at.iso8601 %>" class="text-xs text-cream-600">
              <%= l(entry.created_at, format: :long) %>
            </time>
          </div>

          <%# ⚠️ Tier LABELS, not the raw keys. Actors::SelectAiPackage stores the two
              packages as labels but the two tiers as KEYS, so the sentence read
              'Leistungsstufe von "fast" auf "thorough" gewechselt' while every other
              surface says "Schnell & günstig" / "Gründlich". On the one page sold as an
              AVV record that is the most conspicuous line there is.

              Fixed at the READER, not the writer, deliberately: rows written before this
              exist and cannot be rewritten, and Activity#message merges its options OVER
              the stored parameters — so the same call repairs old and new rows alike.
              The label comes from the package the entry points at (operators may rename
              a rung), falling back to the shipped defaults and finally to the key, which
              is still better than nothing for a package that no longer exists. %>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-cream-900"><%= entry.message(**tier_labels(entry)) %></p>

          <% parameters = entry.parameters || {} %>
          <% from_jurisdiction = parameters['from_jurisdiction'] %>
          <% to_jurisdiction = parameters['to_jurisdiction'] %>
          <%# Only when it MOVED. A row repeating the same jurisdiction on both sides
              would train the reader to skip the one line they are here for.
              ⚠️ Both sides go through .presence, and BOTH resolve their label through
              'blank'. An earlier version asked `to_jurisdiction.present?` and was
              therefore silent about the direction that matters most: LEAVING a
              jurisdiction. Actors::SelectAiPackage writes to_jurisdiction from
              `package&.effective_jurisdiction`, and the "Eigene Konfiguration" card posts
              a BLANK package id (E1-C) — so a switch away from a non-EU package stored
              from: 'non_eu', to: nil and rendered nothing. For a trail whose stated
              purpose is proving when processing abroad began AND ENDED, the end is the
              half nobody can reconstruct from anywhere else. Same reason a package whose
              jurisdiction column is empty (allow_blank) must not silence the row. %>
          <% if from_jurisdiction.presence != to_jurisdiction.presence &&
                (from_jurisdiction.present? || to_jurisdiction.present?) %>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-cream-600">
              <%= t('views.organisations.ai_overview.protocol.jurisdiction_change',
                    from: t("views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.jurisdictions.#{from_jurisdiction.presence || 'blank'}"),
                    to: t("views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.jurisdictions.#{to_jurisdiction.presence || 'blank'}")) %>
            </p>
          <% end %>

          <%# The operating half of the same decision, and the only field in the payload
              that cannot be reconstructed from the two package rows afterwards. %>
          <% if parameters['embedding_lane_moved'] %>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-cream-600">
              <i class="bi bi-arrow-repeat mr-1"></i><%= t('views.organisations.ai_overview.protocol.reindex_triggered') %>
            </p>
          <% end %>
        </li>
      <% end %>
    </ol>

    <%# The COMPACT nav, not shared/_pagination_nav. The reason given here used to be a
        DEFECT: ApplicationHelper#pagy_url_for resolved its links through url_for, whose
        permit list had no :organisation_id, so it raised below /org/:id. That is fixed —
        it now builds from request.path and carries every query parameter, exactly like
        PaginationHelper#pagination_page_url does.

        Which leaves two builders doing the same job. They are NOT interchangeable yet:
        pagination_page_url takes explicit organisation/project keywords and returns an
        absolute URL for tickets (Turbo compatibility). Merging them is a change to that
        Turbo behaviour and belongs in its own pass. Recorded here rather than silently
        tolerated. The choice below is now about the compact LOOK, nothing else. %>
    <%= render 'shared/pagination_nav_compact', pagy: @pagy, items_per_page: @pagy.limit %>
  <% else %>
    <%# An empty protocol is a statement, not a failure: nothing has been changed since
        the trail started. Saying WHEN it started matters, because entries before P4e /
        S0 do not exist and cannot be reconstructed (L13, "Was heute nicht geschrieben
        wird, existiert nie") — an admin who reads "keine Einträge" as "nichts ist je
        passiert" would draw the wrong conclusion from a correct page. %>
    <div class="rounded-lg border-2 border-dashed border-cream-300 bg-cream-50 p-8 text-center">
      <i class="bi bi-clock-history text-3xl text-cream-400"></i>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm font-bold text-cream-900">
        <%= t('views.organisations.ai_overview.protocol.empty_title') %>
      </p>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-1 max-w-xl text-sm text-cream-600">
        <%= t('views.organisations.ai_overview.protocol.empty_body') %>
      </p>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
